    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 score makes him our clear standout play. **Gunnar Henderson** faces Grant Holmes, who carries an elevated 4.75 xERA, and he benefits significantly from a favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong lineup placement in the three-hole. Following closely, **Drake Baldwin** (72.68) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (70.88) provide elite production anchors. **Drake Baldwin** is particularly well-situated against Trevor Rogers, as his high xwOBA and park advantage help counteract the ambiguity of a pending lineup, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a favorable platoon split against Patrick Sandoval despite the pitcher's respectable metrics.\n\nThe decision to favor **Jackson Merrill** (68.36) over the rest of the bench stems from the aggressive pursuit of category scarcity. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a slow-delivering pitcher in Ryan Gusto, creating an ideal environment for his speed to impact our stolen base targets. Notably, **Nasim Nunez** (64.58) and **Jacob Wilson** (64.36) retain their spots due to similar speed-based upside against vulnerable arms. The most difficult personnel choice was keeping **Miguel Vargas** (60.12) on the bench; while his 0.392 xwOBA is excellent, he was narrowly squeezed out by the more favorable park and SP matchup combinations presented to **Coby Mayo** and **Heliot Ramos**. \n\nManagers should remain alert to the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, as any unexpected shifts in the batting order could dampen the efficiency scores of our top contributors. **Heliot Ramos** is a high-variance play to monitor; while he carries a strong 66.08 score, he faces the toughest pitcher of the day in Grayson Rodriguez. However, the combination of wind blowing out and his position in the heart of the order provides a tactical hedge against Rodriguez's talent. We will continue to monitor weather reports for potential delays, but as it stands, the lineup is optimized to exploit the weaknesses of the opposing staff while aggressively hunting for every available stolen base opportunity.",
